# REQUIRES: python-api, hdf5
# Checkpoints of a Python simulation (D[python-checkpoints]): files whose
# state, additional entries, or bytes were changed, a truncated file, and a
# file that is not one are refused by the bindings with the pointer to
# `.prev`, and by `mdir checkpoint`.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_checkpoints.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide CPU Double mdir %t corrupted | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: corrupted files: refused by the bindings and by mdir checkpoint
# CHECK: checkpoints corrupted CPU Double passed
